r-playground/docker-sabnzbd/compare/nightly-cf5bfa93-ls37...nightly-93997ee9-ls38","upstream":"Harmonize article boundary checks and data truncation\n\n*   The decoder (via `sabctools`) is now responsible for truncating article bodies that exceed their declared `data_size` or the `NzbFile`'s `file_size` when streaming or decoding into memory. It updates `article.decoded_size` and `article.crc32` to reflect the actual bytes kept.\n*   The assembler no longer truncates article data during writing. Instead, it explicitly marks articles as `failed` if their declared `data_begin + data_size` extends beyond the `NzbFile`'s `file_size`, preventing incorrect writes and leaving repair to PAR2.\n*   Offset calculations for skipping or appending articles now consistently rely on `article.decoded_size`, as this is guaranteed to represent the final, truncated size of the data for the file.","upstream_url":"https://github.com/sabnzbd/sabnzbd/commit/93997ee9c9e7223af631dc330f9541fb26a9ae0b"},"config":{"env":["PATH=/lsiopy/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin","PS1=$(whoami)@$(hostname):$(pwd)\\$ ","HOME=/config","TERM=xterm","S6_CMD_WAIT_FOR_SERVICES_MAXTIME=0","S6_VERBOSITY=1","S6_STAGE2_HOOK=/docker-mods","VIRTUAL_ENV=/lsiopy","LSIO_FIRST_PARTY=true","PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8"],"exposed_ports":["8080/tcp"],"volumes":["/config"],"entrypoint":["/init"],"working_dir":"/"},"is_newest":false,"links":{"build":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sabnzbd/builds/nightly-93997ee9-ls38.json","diff":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sabnzbd/builds/nightly-93997ee9-ls38/diff.json","layers":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sabnzbd/builds/nightly-93997ee9-ls38/layers.amd64.json","arm64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sabnzbd/builds/nightly-93997ee9-ls38/layers.arm64.json"},"packages":{},"release":"https://github.com/linuxserver-playground/docker-sabnz